            <title>[LU-21011] sanity-quota test_63: Timeout occurred, last suite running was sanity-quota</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21011</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-quota times out with test_63 as the last test running: "Timeout occurred after N minutes, last suite running was sanity-quota". No ticket links this signature.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen 227 times in 60 days on test_63: 212 on lustre-master and master-next (about 14% of full-part-2 suite runs) plus the b2_16-client interop custom group of reviews 67700 and 69011.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5997d7d4-cbb5-486a-8fd6-7172047afff1" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5997d7d4-cbb5-486a-8fd6-7172047afff1&lt;/a&gt; (change 69011 ps6). Suite started 17:56, test_63 started 19:38 and was still running at the 197 minute timeout. The client had a dd stuck in folio_wait_writeback under ll_fsync, and the suite log shows OST and MDT connection losses and evictions earlier in the run. The same session also fails test_0 with SLOW IO (406 kB/s, quota disabled).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not the same as &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17077" title="sanity-quota test_63: @@@@@@ FAIL: write failed, expect succeed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17077"&gt;LU-17077&lt;/a&gt; (test_63 "write failed, expect succeed").&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69011-ps6-ea8c8a8edd12 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69011" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69011&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
